{"id":"950549c09248b205","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-df-zero-sharp.md","title":"$0^\\sharp$","display":"df-zero-sharp — $0^\\sharp$","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zero-sharp","aliases":["58-df-zero-sharp"],"display":"df-zero-sharp — $0^\\sharp$","depends_on":["[[./58-df-l-hierarchy.md]]","[[../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md]]","[[../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zero-sharp"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zero-sharp</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zero-sharp — <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0^\\sharp\">\\(0^\\sharp\\)</span>"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"cfa29222af6471b2\" href=\"?note=cfa29222af6471b2\" title=\"./58-df-l-hierarchy.md\">58-df-l-hierarchy.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"9a2e92340a207163\" href=\"?note=9a2e92340a207163\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md\">../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"81cabbac7fa4d75d\" href=\"?note=81cabbac7fa4d75d\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md\">../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L_\\bullet:\\mathrm{Ord}\\to V\">\\(L_\\bullet:\\mathrm{Ord}\\to V\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf L\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\">\\(\\mathbf L\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"j:\\mathbf L\\to\\mathbf L\">\\(j:\\mathbf L\\to\\mathbf L\\)</span> are class functions/variables in the metatheory.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Def}\">\\(\\mathrm{Def}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S\\)</span> are as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"9a2e92340a207163\" href=\"?note=9a2e92340a207163\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md\">../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"81cabbac7fa4d75d\" href=\"?note=81cabbac7fa4d75d\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md\">../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S^{(n)}(\\mathcal L_\\in)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S^{(n)}(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\)</span> is the set of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-variable formulas of set theory (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LHierarchy}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{LHierarchy}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\">\\(\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\)</span> are the two metatheoretic predicates defined below.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZeroSharpExists}_S\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZeroSharpExists}_S\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zero\\text{-}sharp\\text{-}l\\text{-}hierarchy\\text{-}meta}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{LHierarchy}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(L_\\bullet)\\leftrightarrow\nL_0=\\emptyset\\land\n\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;(L_{\\alpha+1}=\\mathrm{Def}(L_\\alpha))\\land\n\\forall\\lambda\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S(\\lambda)\\to L_\\lambda=\\bigcup_{\\alpha&lt;\\lambda}L_\\alpha\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zero\\text{-}sharp\\text{-}l\\text{-}hierarchy\\text{-}meta}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{LHierarchy}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(L_\\bullet)\\leftrightarrow\nL_0=\\emptyset\\land\n\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;(L_{\\alpha+1}=\\mathrm{Def}(L_\\alpha))\\land\n\\forall\\lambda\\in\\mathrm{Ord}\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S(\\lambda)\\to L_\\lambda=\\bigcup_{\\alpha&lt;\\lambda}L_\\alpha\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zero\\text{-}sharp\\text{-}elementary\\text{-}class\\text{-}embedding}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(j,\\mathbf L)\\leftrightarrow\nj:\\mathbf L\\to\\mathbf L\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S^{(n)}(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\;\n\\forall\\bar a\\in\\mathbf L^n\\;\\Bigl(\n(\\mathbf L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar a]\\leftrightarrow\n(\\mathbf L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[j\\circ\\bar a]\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zero\\text{-}sharp\\text{-}elementary\\text{-}class\\text{-}embedding}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(j,\\mathbf L)\\leftrightarrow\nj:\\mathbf L\\to\\mathbf L\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S^{(n)}(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\;\n\\forall\\bar a\\in\\mathbf L^n\\;\\Bigl(\n(\\mathbf L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[\\bar a]\\leftrightarrow\n(\\mathbf L,\\in)\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\varphi[j\\circ\\bar a]\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zero\\text{-}sharp} \\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ZeroSharpExists}_S\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists L_\\bullet\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\exists\\mathbf L\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\exists j\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LHierarchy}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(L_\\bullet)\\land\n\\mathbf L=\\bigcup_{\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ord}}L_\\alpha\\land\n\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(j,\\mathbf L)\\land\nj\\neq\\operatorname{id}_{\\mathbf L}\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zero\\text{-}sharp} \\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n\\mathrm{ZeroSharpExists}_S\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists L_\\bullet\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\exists\\mathbf L\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\exists j\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LHierarchy}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(L_\\bullet)\\land\n\\mathbf L=\\bigcup_{\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ord}}L_\\alpha\\land\n\\mathrm{ElementaryClassEmbedding}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(j,\\mathbf L)\\land\nj\\neq\\operatorname{id}_{\\mathbf L}\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The nontrivial embedding is a metatheoretic class embedding of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>; the set-coded elementary-embedding predicate is not applied to a proper class.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0^\\sharp\">\\(0^\\sharp\\)</span> is the real coding the complete theory of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf L\">\\(\\mathbf L\\)</span> with a sequence of Silver indiscernibles.</li>\n<li>The existence of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0^\\sharp\">\\(0^\\sharp\\)</span> implies that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1\">\\(\\omega_1\\)</span> is not absolute between <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0^\\sharp\">\\(0^\\sharp\\)</span> exists if and only if there are uncountably many Silver indiscernibles</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"./58-df-l-hierarchy.md","status":"resolved","id":"cfa29222af6471b2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[./58-df-l-hierarchy.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"9a2e92340a207163","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"81cabbac7fa4d75d","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"9a2e92340a207163","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Def}$ and $\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S$ are as in [[../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md]] and [[../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md]].","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"81cabbac7fa4d75d","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Def}$ and $\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S$ are as in [[../batch19/58-df-def-operator.md]] and [[../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md]].","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"r